Call `Flag` on the executing `*Command`:

```go
f := cmd.Flag("flag-name")
if f == nil {
    // flag not found
}
```

`(*Command).Flag(name)` first checks `c.Flags().Lookup(name)`, then searches persistent flags up the command tree (`command.go:1794–1803`). `ExecuteC` also returns the command that executed as `cmd *Command` (`command.go:1052`).----- DEVELOPMENT ANSWER KEY -----
